{
    "word": "otherworldly",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "2a3f19ec-f182-34a1-9a7b-0cfffc3284c3",
                "word": "otherworldly",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d005666b-06c8-4853-be7d-e22e2f278135",
                        "entry_id": "2a3f19ec-f182-34a1-9a7b-0cfffc3284c3",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more otherworldly"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "635d4e10-945b-439f-8e4e-da4bb4883bc0",
                        "entry_id": "2a3f19ec-f182-34a1-9a7b-0cfffc3284c3",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most otherworldly"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72573f81-bc5a-37d9-940d-22c34f2d7896",
                        "entry_id": "2a3f19ec-f182-34a1-9a7b-0cfffc3284c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, concerned with, or preoccupied with a world different from the tangible world, especially a fantasy, imaginary, or mystical world."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0124c2db-e2f3-4df6-8479-d3901011e7ef",
                                "sense_id": "72573f81-bc5a-37d9-940d-22c34f2d7896",
                                "text": "In Just My Type: A Book about Fonts (2010) Simon Garfield describes [Edward] Johnston as 'a gaunt fine-boned man with a full moustache', and there's a picture of him at work with a quill pen that makes him look as other-worldly as a medieval sprite."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0e01e4b-a907-3d89-bd10-858e8d33d5d8",
                        "entry_id": "2a3f19ec-f182-34a1-9a7b-0cfffc3284c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, concerned with, or preoccupied with a world different from the tangible world, especially a fantasy, imaginary, or mystical world.",
                            "Odd and unfamiliar; strange, uncanny, weird."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07d7aa4e-eb38-4ff0-9fe5-5f3e2fb24499",
                                "sense_id": "d0e01e4b-a907-3d89-bd10-858e8d33d5d8",
                                "text": "He had not seen cricket played since the war began; it seemed almost other-worldly, with the click of the bats, and the shrill young voices, under the distant drone of that sky-hornet threshing along to Hendon."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d6c5d92-d582-4ca3-b196-a9cf0fc97aac",
                                "sense_id": "d0e01e4b-a907-3d89-bd10-858e8d33d5d8",
                                "text": "An almost otherworldly resilience has characterized the 40-year arc of the Clintons' political lives, a well-documented pattern of dazzling success, shattering setback and inevitable recovery."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa027325-42a3-4850-96cd-9d02aef567eb",
                                "sense_id": "d0e01e4b-a907-3d89-bd10-858e8d33d5d8",
                                "text": "“Hey, Rick.” “Oh, hey, kiddo. How's your Saturday?” “You know, super chill. W-W-Whatcha doin'?” “Eh, nothing adventurous. You know that race of Underground Dwelling Cannibal Horse People that we're always fighting?” “Yeah, the CHUDs. W-W-What about 'em? “Well, don't tell anybody, but I'm working on a bioweapon to use against them, so I got this barrel of horse semen from your mom's hospital and I'm just gonna, you know, subject it to some otherworldly forces.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1913613-21f2-4ffd-91d7-b6f0ba1fea33",
                                "sense_id": "d0e01e4b-a907-3d89-bd10-858e8d33d5d8",
                                "text": "The sudden inundation from the remnants of Ida transformed familiar scenes of life in New York into otherworldly and waterlogged chaos on Wednesday night."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a8df9cab-0fad-4e08-872a-e138e091252e",
                                "sense_id": "d0e01e4b-a907-3d89-bd10-858e8d33d5d8",
                                "text": "“David [Bowie] used to say he would sell his soul to be famous,” she says. “But he was also otherworldly – and you couldn’t take your eyes off him.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb75b15b-ac1e-3d14-a829-6fa380ee1011",
                        "entry_id": "2a3f19ec-f182-34a1-9a7b-0cfffc3284c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, concerned with, or preoccupied with spiritual matters."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dfedbe15-7660-4048-abfe-e8832693a788",
                                "sense_id": "eb75b15b-ac1e-3d14-a829-6fa380ee1011",
                                "text": "Every religion that becomes ascendant, in so far as it is not otherworldly, must necessarily set its stamp upon the methods and administration of the law."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e82c1e9a-eebf-4341-9641-11556f65202f",
                                "sense_id": "eb75b15b-ac1e-3d14-a829-6fa380ee1011",
                                "text": "[Leo] Tolstoy was not a saint, but he tried very hard to make himself into a saint, and the standards he applied to literature were other-worldly ones."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c10bc03e-c325-487e-b18e-7ffdd07d4cf1",
                                "sense_id": "eb75b15b-ac1e-3d14-a829-6fa380ee1011",
                                "text": "[Simphiwe] Dana has the otherworldly temperament of a mystic."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "98053278-81bf-3d43-ae88-92e47f79da0f",
                        "entry_id": "2a3f19ec-f182-34a1-9a7b-0cfffc3284c3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or relating to the imagination or intellect."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "obsolete",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
